{"payload":{"debate_id":"eebfa022-fec6-4d6f-9c04-2437e3affcf2","judge_seat":"haiku","judge_api_model":"anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5","verdict_raw":"{"verdict_tag":"HELD","defense_standing":"PROP-DEPENDENT","challenge_standing":"PROP-DEPENDENT","conceded_links":0,"challenger_conceded_links":0,"counted_premises_defender":[],"counted_premises_challenger":[],"reasoning":"Line 1 (verdict): HELD. The defender's chain D1-D5 was declared in [CR1] and carried through [CR2]-[CR4]. The challenger's premises against it (the list closing [DR2]) were pressed with witnesses; the defender's [CR3] answered each premise by re-exhibiting layers and answering the pressed verses, and the challenger's objections ran mostly to presses of words and the 'house does not show seed' point, which the defender answered with Galatians 4:4 and Matthew 1:16/Numbers 1:18 read together. No defender link was shown by the challenger to be refuted from the text with a proven, unanswered press, and no defender link was withdrawn. The [CR3] link round exhibited layers for each defender link.\nRESULT: DEFENDER WINS -- the defender's chain, read together with Matthew 1:18-20, 25, Luke 1:34-35 and Isaiah 7:14 with Matthew 1:22-23, stands against the challenger's reading, which rests on presses (Matthew 1:19, Romans 1:3, Acts 2:30) whose meanings the defender answered in [CR3] without a shown failure of fit.\nCLAUSE: HELD-1 -- n=5 w=0 k=0\nKEYSTONE: D5 -- STANDS -- the conclusion link stands: Matthew 1:18, 20 with Luke 1:34-35 exhibit [L1]-[L3] footing, and no CONCEDED or UNEXHIBITED count falls on it.\nDEFENSE STANDING: PROP-DEPENDENT -- L=6 c=0 -- the challenger listed six premises against the defender and the defender exhibited layers for each in [CR3]; the standing is PROP-DEPENDENT rather than SELF-SUPPORTED because several defender [L4] steps (e.g. 'Joseph was not the biological father' from 'before they came together') rest on inference that the challenger contested.\nCHALLENGE STANDING: PROP-DEPENDENT -