e seed of David according to the flesh', using the word 'made' rather than begotten of a man\" -- NOT A REQUIREMENT -- rebuts [DR3] \"Romans 1:3 requires seed of David according to the flesh\".\nCONTRADICTIONS: NONE FOUND.\nOUT-OF-ROUND CONCESSIONS:\nNONE\nDEFENDER CHAIN MARK: STRAINED -- D2 rests on an inferred maternal route for 'seed of David' that the record's rows do not state in words.\nCHALLENGER CHAIN MARK: STRAINED -- the challenger's alternative reading (Joseph as begetter) rests on the Numbers 1:2 and Luke 2:48 registers, which are read as legal rather than biological.\nRULING CARDS: D5 -- STANDS. CLAIM: the conception was by the Holy Ghost prior to marital union. NAMED BY: \"before they came together, she was found with child of the Holy Ghost\" (Matthew 1:18). RULE: Commitment 3 -- \"Scripture does not contradict itself.\" APPLIED: the rule requires the challenger's readings to agree with the Matthew 1:18 row; the record shows the Matthew 1:19-20 presses answered; so the link stands."}

